# Pretty profile URLs on Netlify.
#
# A static export cannot have a real /u/<username> route (generateStaticParams
# would need every username at build time), so rewrite it onto the query-param
# route the app actually ships. VerceL users: the equivalent lives in
# vercel.json — "rewrites": [{ "source": "/u/:u", "destination": "/user?u=:u" }]
/u/*  /user?u=:splat  200

# SPA fallback for unknown paths (a static export renders each route to its own
# .html, so this only catches genuinely missing paths).
/*  /404.html  404
